-- ── story 5-2a: client webhooks ──────────────────────────────────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the three tables and their indexes) and
-- hand-amended around the generated part: the fail-fast guard, `IF NOT
-- EXISTS` on every table and index (guide §3), the CHECKs, the RLS policies,
-- the widened notifications source vocabulary and the post-migration probe
-- (drizzle-kit is blind to CHECKs and RLS; `bun run db:generate` afterwards
-- reports "No schema changes").
--
--   webhook_endpoints   — a client's HTTPS endpoint: its normalised URL, the
--                         event types it subscribes to, the sealed signing
--                         secret (and the previous one for 24 h after a
--                         rotation), the auto-disable counters, a soft delete.
--   webhook_events      — one frozen v1 envelope per (event type, subject):
--                         the GRN id or the order id.
--   webhook_deliveries  — one event to one endpoint: pending → sending →
--                         succeeded | failed, or held while its endpoint is
--                         auto-disabled for failing.
--   notifications       — `notifications_source_type_check` gains
--                         `webhook-disabled`, re-added NOT VALID (A9): the new
--                         list is a superset of the old one, so every existing
--                         row passes by construction; VALIDATE is a later
--                         migration's (PENDING deploy).
--
-- No data statements: purely additive, so no pre-flight. The three tables are
-- new and empty, so their CHECKs and indexes cost nothing; the notifications
-- CHECK is NOT VALID, so it takes no scan.

-- ── 0. fail-fast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'webhook_endpoints'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0100: webhook_endpoints already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
	IF NOT EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'client_charges'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0100 is out of order: client_charges does not exist — 0099 must be applied first.';
	END IF;
END $$;
